# A fixed fallback opens the game menu whatever the bindings are (#326; written before the implementation): the LEFT
# controller's menu button held about 2 s - not part of the layout, not rebindable. On the simulated Index, with a
# binding set that has no menu entry, saved into vr-controls-index.ini as the VR settings page saves it and read back
# as a start reads it: the radial menu (the only way to the game menu, D-042) moved to the left trackpad, the menu
# event unbound. The right B then opens nothing, a tap of the left menu button is no long press, a 2.5 s hold opens
# the game menu, and the VR settings' reset to default is reachable from it.
# The Index has no menu button the game can read (SteamVR keeps the system button): the simulated button is pressed
# through the channel. Which button the Index uses is the owner's choice (the contract's do_not_decide).
#
# Assumes (the worker adds them to status.json, src/core/CommandChannel.cpp, named exactly):
#   vr.input.menuFallback.control  (text)    the fallback's control as vr::controlName writes it: left.menu
#   vr.input.menuFallback.holdMs   (number)  how long it is held before the game menu opens, in ms: 2000
#   vr.input.menuFallback.opens    (count)   how often the long press opened the game menu since the start
# Self-contained: it ends with the default layout and no saved file (CI runs every sequence in one user directory).
@sim idle
@args --loadlevel 10

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 120 60s
@assert vr.input.controllers eq index
vr-input default
@frames 2
@assert vr.input.remapped eq false
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert vr.input.menuFallback.control eq left.menu
@assert vr.input.menuFallback.holdMs eq 2000
@remember opens0 vr.input.menuFallback.opens

# The binding set without a menu entry: the radial menu captured on the left trackpad (saved), read back as at a start
menu pause
@until menuMode eq mainmenu 10s
menu vr
@until menuPage eq vr 10s
@frames 10
vr-input capture radial_right
@frames 2
vr-input tap left.trackpad
@until vr.input.capture.state eq done 5s
menu resume
@until menuMode eq ingame 10s
@mark
vr-input reload
@log \[vr\] input: controllers index - layout saved for index
@until vr.input.remapped eq true 5s
@assert vr.input.layout.radial_right eq left.trackpad
@assert vr.input.layout.radial_left eq none
@assert vr.input.layout.menu eq none

# The right B opens nothing now; a tap of the left menu button is no long press
vr-input tap right.b
@wait 1000
@assert menuMode eq ingame
vr-input tap left.menu
@wait 1000
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert vr.input.menuFallback.opens eq {opens0}

# The long press: the left menu button held 2.5 s opens the game menu
vr-input down left.menu
@wait 2500
vr-input up left.menu
@until menuMode eq mainmenu 5s
@assert vr.input.menuFallback.opens eq {opens0+1}

# From it the VR settings' reset to default: the right B's radial menu is back, the saved file gone
menu vr
@until menuPage eq vr 10s
vr-input default
@frames 2
@assert vr.input.remapped eq false
@assert vr.input.layout.radial_right eq right.b
menu resume
@until menuMode eq ingame 10s
@assert errors eq 0
